        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "fa0e44ca-215c-31b1-a14d-427527db6c0b",
                "word": "philtre",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d9af97d9-8919-439b-9448-135507c91d40",
                        "entry_id": "fa0e44ca-215c-31b1-a14d-427527db6c0b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "philtres"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ea22449e-f7f4-3ce9-a7b3-8b4097e292b2",
                        "entry_id": "fa0e44ca-215c-31b1-a14d-427527db6c0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Breuvage, drogue, qu’on suppose propre à donner de l’amour, ou, en général, à provoquer quelque passion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "de224150-658b-4494-a8e0-88ee1e254e07",
                                "sense_id": "ea22449e-f7f4-3ce9-a7b3-8b4097e292b2",
                                "text": "Les amoureux savent leur trouver des philtres, répondit madame Mignon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4944eb8a-cc6c-4995-a05c-f7f22ad931e7",
                                "sense_id": "ea22449e-f7f4-3ce9-a7b3-8b4097e292b2",
                                "text": "On peut donc continuer à boire de l'eau de Seltz sans crainte, […]. C'est un digestif, un stimulant de l'appétit, un philtre merveilleux qui donne à un vin médiocre les qualités d'un bon cru, et fait plus contre l'ivrognerie que toutes les Sociétés de tempérance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96699127-4bf8-41d9-81fe-04450865bb5d",
                                "sense_id": "ea22449e-f7f4-3ce9-a7b3-8b4097e292b2",
                                "text": "Il avait des dollars dans sa poche ; ‬la nuit s’ouvrait, tous les philtres allaient couler, il allait plaire à tous et toutes.\nLa drogue qui l’isolait de tout contact, qui le soustrayait à toute épreuve, l’avait confirmé dans cette imagination immobile."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "274f024f-fdc2-42d3-aba3-c50f6b66e967",
                                "sense_id": "ea22449e-f7f4-3ce9-a7b3-8b4097e292b2",
                                "text": "Qu’est-ce alors que le philtre ? C’est l’alibi de la passion. C’est ce qui permet aux malheureux amants de dire : « Vous voyez que je n’y suis pour rien, vous voyez que c’est plus fort que moi »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37bb6611-cc09-4188-bb08-5f7943a6622a",
                                "sense_id": "ea22449e-f7f4-3ce9-a7b3-8b4097e292b2",
                                "text": "Jadis le sorcier, le magicien, le jeteur de sort faisaient grand usage du crapaud. […] On le cuisait dans des chaudières pour lui, soutirer des poisons ou des philtres."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d979a488-5997-37c7-b5f4-6736240383c2",
                        "entry_id": "fa0e44ca-215c-31b1-a14d-427527db6c0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chez l’Humain, repli en forme de gouttière qui relie la base du nez à la lèvre supérieure, au niveau de l’arc de Cupidon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88a11b8e-8b84-44ac-9376-e1b5503c3e65",
                                "sense_id": "d979a488-5997-37c7-b5f4-6736240383c2",
                                "text": "La gouttière qui se trouve sur la lèvre, au-dessous de la colonne, s’appelle philtre, et toute la partie de la lèvre supérieure venant après le nez, région sous-nasale; ensuite viennent les deux lèvres, dont les extrémités s'appellent avant-lèvres, et la commissure avant-bouche."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "61eb4527-81ab-439b-9971-54fef2c5fc0c",
                        "source_entry_id": "fa0e44ca-215c-31b1-a14d-427527db6c0b",
                        "source_sense_id": "ea22449e-f7f4-3ce9-a7b3-8b4097e292b2",
                        "source_sense_description": "Breuvage provoquant l’amour",
                        "target_lang_word": "philtre",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "philtre",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e131b2d6-f7b0-3ede-9d00-da686eb41480",
                                        "entry_id": "c814b123-91f1-3a49-9575-0b432ab3fc19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of philter (“kind of potion”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e053e7b-a74b-4860-b18e-d1f32b594c76",
                                                "sense_id": "e131b2d6-f7b0-3ede-9d00-da686eb41480",
                                                "text": "[…] Bring hippomanes, / Fierce philtre from the frantic, brooding mare!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d4385ea-c928-4b28-afd3-1d4f14ebe6f0",
                                                "sense_id": "e131b2d6-f7b0-3ede-9d00-da686eb41480",
                                                "text": "What wine, what drug, what philtre known of man / Will drown this ancient foe, / Ruthless and ravenous as a courtesan, / Sure as an ant, and slow?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97da7ef9-c9c8-49be-aa7e-a8acfc3f7309",
                                                "sense_id": "e131b2d6-f7b0-3ede-9d00-da686eb41480",
                                                "text": "Old witches in the cities and country-side throve upon the sale of death spells and love philtres. They also made a trade of abortificants, and frequently practised the whiles of the procuress."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dffa1b2f-7ac1-400f-bc94-4cdd022f9342",
                                                "sense_id": "e131b2d6-f7b0-3ede-9d00-da686eb41480",
                                                "text": "In the desperate search for amatory satisfactions, the most monstrous ingredients have throughout the ages, been sought and compounded into electuaries and pastilles, philtres and ointments."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "philtre",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6bb126f-60a2-3820-bb48-6625ba2659dd",
                                        "entry_id": "ef09d959-67d8-3842-b6bd-1b2938f73510",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of philter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9973fb39-317e-4004-b69f-57aa27b0119c",
                                                "sense_id": "e6bb126f-60a2-3820-bb48-6625ba2659dd",
                                                "text": "The friendship of the men he took amiably and modestly, though no man was his superior of all the king's men in strength or skill. The friendship of the women he let go by him, also very modestly but always with decision. There were many that longed to knock at the door of his heart and enter in, and there were some that showed their longing, most notably of all the beautiful Esclaramonde of Bayonne, whom most men worshipped for her dark, imperious loveliness, and whom all the women, her rivals, hated for a witch, and upbraided beneath their breaths for her skill in philtres."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24d7b438-c4bd-4a1e-9918-721cdfcc47b2",
                        "source_entry_id": "fa0e44ca-215c-31b1-a14d-427527db6c0b",
